learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:1: trailing whitespace.
+Feature: Recognize the availability and consistency limit after total destination loss
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:2: trailing whitespace.
+  As an operator rehearsing A-S120, packet SC-S120, parent D-S120
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:3: trailing whitespace.
+  I remove only the two fixed fictional destinations in the lesson
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:4: trailing whitespace.
+  So that a correct negative verification never becomes zero-downtime migration success
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:5: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:6: trailing whitespace.
+  Background:
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:7: trailing whitespace.
+    Given the banner is "Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result"
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:8: trailing whitespace.
+    And all destinations, regions, capacity, state, requests, effects and durations are fixed teaching data
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:9: trailing whitespace.
+    And fictional paths origin-a and origin-b each have capacity 2, state revision 7 and writer epoch 3
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:10: trailing whitespace.
+    And the supported envelope requires at least one reachable consistent path for demand 2
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:11: trailing whitespace.
+    And the synthetic request budget is 100 milliseconds, not an Azure threshold
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:12: trailing whitespace.
+    And no resource, process, network, cloud or shared harness is changed by a lesson action
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:13: trailing whitespace.
+
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:14: trailing whitespace.
+  Scenario: A surviving viable destination is a positive control, not total-loss success
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:15: trailing whitespace.
+    When I observe the supported fixture
learning/S120/evidence/red/total-loss-feature.source:16: trailing whitespace.
+    And confirm removal of origin-a
